"""tempest_shallows story pass (22 Nov 2026), to docs/quest_writing_standard.md. Where the giver's speech sat in the accept
line and the journal showed a summary or narration, the speech is now the description and the accept line a new short
beat; the rest were written fresh. Turn-ins untouched."""

STORY = {
    'tmp_off_the_boat': (
        "Can you take this up to Quartermaster Durn for me? I can't leave the jetty while there's a boat tied up.\n\nIt's the manifest for the boat you came in on. Durn won't open the stores until he's checked it against what was landed.\n\nHe's under the big awning with the barrels, just along the shore to the south-east. Tell him the count's right.",
        "If he starts counting the barrels again, let him. He's happier when he's counting.",
    ),
    'tmp_teeth_on_the_trunk_road': (
        "Nobody could land on this island until the sea route opened three years ago. Now everything we land goes east along the trunk road through the Green Belt, and the road isn't safe.\n\nThe Greenbelt Raptors hunt it in packs. The Canopy Panthers wait in the trees above it and drop on whoever's at the back. I've lost porters to both.\n\nThe Green Belt is the jungle east of the landing. Follow the road in and kill what you find on it.",
        "Walk in the middle of the road, not the edge. The panthers pick off whoever's closest to the trees.",
    ),
    'tmp_the_road_to_the_wharf': (
        "I need my tally taken to Harbourmaster Skezz in Cinderwharf, and you've shown you can look after yourself.\n\nShe runs the berths over there. Four barges left this jetty since spring and never reached her, and she wants my list of which ones.\n\nTake the trunk road east through the Green Belt, then the east road north round the mountain into the Ashen Reach. Keep north along the shore until you reach the town gate. The country past the mountain is harder than this, so be ready for it.",
        'Skezz will want to argue about my numbers. Let her, and then make her sign for it.',
    ),
    'tmp_crab_for_the_pot': (
        "I've got forty people to feed and the supply boat brought me flour and salt.\n\nThere's plenty of food out in the shallows. The Bargebreaker Crabs are as big as a handcart and a claw will feed a table, but they fight.\n\nGo east along the trunk road and take the strand road down to the water. Bring me the claws and I'll get them cooking.",
        'Twist the claws off at the joint. If you cut them, I lose half the meat.',
    ),
    'tmp_carried_up_by_hand': (
        "Somebody's been stealing crates off the ruin road at night, and I know who.\n\nThere are dwarves camped in the forecourt of Khaz Varun's Gate, south-east of here at the end of the road. They went into the city and came out wrong, and now they won't leave. The big ones, the Gate-Squatter Brawlers, come up the road after dark and take whatever my porters put down.\n\nGet my crates back. You'll have to deal with the Brawlers to do it.",
        "Check the seals on the crates when you get them back. I'll want to know if they've been opened.",
    ),
    'tmp_mother_canopy': (
        "I've lost three porters this month on the trunk road, and it was the last one in the line every time.\n\nThe woodcutters say it's a panther twice the size of the others. They call her Mother Canopy. She hunts the stretch of road under the thickest trees in the Green Belt, east of the landing.\n\nShe doesn't show herself to just anyone, but she'll come for someone who goes looking. Please kill her.",
        "Walk at the back of the line if you want her to find you. That's who she takes.",
    ),
    'tmp_what_its_worth': (
        "I'm supposed to put a value on this whole island for the underwriters. Nobody could reach it before the change, so nobody's done it before.\n\nThere are three places I haven't been able to stand in. The first is the heart of the Green Belt, east of here along the trunk road. The second is further east, where the strand road meets the water. The third is the pass on the Scoured Slope, north-west of the landing up the west road.\n\nGo to each one, have a good look, and come back and tell me what's there.",
        "Write down what you'd pay for each place, if it were yours. I'd like a second opinion.",
    ),
    'tmp_preachers_in_the_forecourt': (
        "I can't survey the forecourt of Khaz Varun's Gate because the squatters keep setting fire to my equipment.\n\nThe ones doing it are the Gate-Squatter Ashpreachers. They stand in the rubble shouting at the arch, and they throw fire at strangers. They also carry slates with writing on them. If it's a claim on the city, the underwriters need to know.\n\nThe forecourt is south-east of here at the end of the ruin road. Deal with the Ashpreachers and bring me some of their slates.",
        "Wrap the slates in something. The underwriters won't read a cracked one.",
    ),
    'tmp_bitterbark': (
        "I've run out of painkillers, and the boat won't bring more for a month.\n\nBefore I came through I had a whole cabinet of them. Here I've got bandages and clean water. The woodcutters tell me the Ashfur Gorillas in the Green Belt chew a grey bark and put it on their burns, and the burned ones are climbing again in a day.\n\nThe Green Belt is east of the landing along the trunk road. The gorillas carry the chewed bark with them. I'd like to try it.",
        "Don't chew any yourself on the way back. I'll test it before anyone tries it.",
    ),
    'tmp_snapper_fat': (
        "Most of what I treat here is burns. Before I came through I'd have ordered dressings from the hospital stores, but here I've got to make them, and I need a clean fat that keeps.\n\nButter goes off in a day in this heat and lamp oil makes a wound worse. The cook says the fat under a Shallows Snapper's shell stays fresh for weeks.\n\nThe snappers are out in the Tempest Shallows, east along the trunk road and down the strand road. Watch their beaks.",
        'Bring it in a jar with the lid tight. The flies here find everything.',
    ),
    'tmp_hulls_and_ribs': (
        "I built boats in Booty Bay until the sea route opened three years ago and the Ashclaim offered me more. I need seasoned timber for barge hulls, and the jungle wood is too green. It warps before the pitch has dried, and I can't use it.\n\nThe best timber on the island is in the old wrecks out in the Tempest Shallows, but the Wreckpicker Murlocs strip the wrecks and carry the planks off to build with.\n\nGo east along the trunk road and down the strand road to the water, and take the timber off the murlocs.",
        "Bring me oak if you can tell it. It's the dark grain, and it's heavy for its size.",
    ),
    'tmp_the_barge_eater': (
        "I've found out what's been sinking my barges.\n\nOne of my crew watched it from the beach. A loaded barge was crossing the bay and a huge crab came up under it and put a claw through the hull. The jetty hands call it The Barge-Eater.\n\nIt lives in the deep part of the Tempest Shallows, south-east of here past the last of the wrecks. It comes up for people who go out hunting it. Please kill it before I lose another crew.",
        "Stay off the sandbar when it surfaces. It'll come up under whatever's standing still.",
    ),
    'tmp_clear_the_slip': (
        "My barges need a clear channel out of the bay, and the bottom's crawling with things that slow them down.\n\nThe Shallows Snappers bite at the steering oars and the Bargebreaker Crabs grab hold of the hulls. A slow barge is an easy target for worse.\n\nThe channel runs out through the Tempest Shallows, east along the trunk road and down the strand road. Wade out and clear what you find.",
        "Go at high tide. You'll be able to see more of them in the clear water.",
    ),
    'tmp_the_unhoused': (
        "The squatters in the forecourt follow one of their own, and I knew him before he went in.\n\nHis name's Borrik. He was a mason, and the Thane sent him down with the first party. He came out after six days and wouldn't go further than the forecourt. He says the city turned him away, and the others call him Borrik the Unhoused.\n\nHe keeps to the broken ground south and east of here. He'll come out for someone who's hunting him. I can't leave my post, and I don't think I could do it anyway.",
        "If he says anything about the city before the end, remember it. I'd like to know what turned him away.",
    ),
    'tmp_whelps_in_the_vents': (
        "Khaz Varun gets its air through shafts that come out high on the mountain, and something's nesting in them.\n\nMy family kept those vents clear for nine generations. Now the Ashwing Whelps roost in the shaft mouths because the stone's warm, and they've filled them with ash and bones.\n\nThe vents open onto the Scoured Slope, north of here up the west road. Clear out the whelps for me.",
        'Pull the bones out of the shaft mouths after. They block the draw as much as the nests do.',
    ),
    'tmp_nine_generations': (
        "You keep looking at that arch. Ask me about it before you do anything about it.\n\nWhen you're done, I've got a favour to ask. I keep a book of everyone who goes through the gate and everyone who comes back. The Thane hasn't seen it in two months because nobody will carry it to him.\n\nHe's in Cinderwharf on the north-east shore. Take the trunk road east, the east road north round the mountain, and follow the shore north to the town.",
        "Ask the Thane to sign the back page when he's read it. That's how my father did it.",
    ),
    'tmp_prospecting_by_gizzard': (
        "Nobody's prospected this island since the gate opened three years ago, and I want to find the truesilver without digging up half of it.\n\nBasilisks swallow stones to grind their food, and they pick them up wherever they walk. If there's truesilver in a basilisk's gizzard, there's a seam somewhere on its route.\n\nThe Rubble Basilisks are thickest round Khaz Varun's Gate, south-east of here. Bring me the stones from their gizzards.",
        "Rinse the stones before you bring them in. I'd rather not handle what's on them.",
    ),
    'tmp_the_colour_of_the_rock': (
        "Truesilver usually shows in a blue-grey rock, and I can see two patches of that colour from here.\n\nBoth are up on the Scoured Slope. One's north-west, above the west road, and the other's north-east, above the east road. The Cinderslope Flame Spirits gather on that kind of rock and I can't get close.\n\nGo up to both outcrops and take a good look. You'll have to deal with the Flame Spirits first.",
        "Chip a piece off each outcrop if you can. The colour fades once it's out of the ground.",
    ),
    'tmp_what_grows_back': (
        "I'm studying a strip of the Scoured Slope where plants are growing back on the bare ash.\n\nI did the same work in the hills near Quito before the change, after the eruptions there. Here the first thing to grow back is a small red fern. The Ashscree Scorpions burrow under it and tear the roots up.\n\nThe slope is north of here, where the trees stop. If you can thin out the scorpions I'll be able to finish my notes for the season.",
        "Watch where you put your feet on the slope. I've spent two seasons getting those ferns to come back.",
    ),
    'tmp_pressed_and_labelled': (
        "The Ashclaim pays me to tell them which plants here are worth money, and I've pressed forty of them between these boards.\n\nAlchemist Pell in Cinderwharf decides what the Ashclaim buys, so the press needs to reach him flat and dry.\n\nTake the east road north round the mountain into the Ashen Reach and follow the shore north to the town. He's by the salvage yard. Please ask him to send the boards back, it's the only press I've got.",
        'Carry it flat, with the strap done up. If the boards slip, the labels go everywhere.',
    ),
    'tmp_my_boots': (
        "I went out to the near wreck in my good sea boots and came back without them.\n\nIt's the wreck you can see sticking up to the south-east. A Bargebreaker Crab got one boot and another one got the second while I was getting away.\n\nThey were made for me in Booty Bay and they've got brass toes. The crabs round that wreck will still have them. Please get them back for me.",
        "Don't fight them in the water if you can help it. That's how I lost the second one.",
    ),
    'tmp_whats_still_aboard': (
        "There are two big wrecks a long way out that still had cargo when they went down.\n\nOne is south-east of here at the edge of the deep water. The other is further south, past the sandbar. The cargo was sealed in small casks, and the Wreckpicker Murlocs have been carrying them off.\n\nGo out to both wrecks and see what's left, and get the casks back from the murlocs. We'll split whatever's inside.",
        "Don't open the casks out there. Bring them back sealed and we'll do it together.",
    ),
    'tmp_pay_chit': (
        "You turn the brass tag over in your fingers. The Brawler was wearing it on a string round its neck. It's a pay chit from the Ashclaim stores, the kind every porter at the landing gets, and it's stamped with a number. The string is new, but the brass is worn smooth from somebody's thumb. Quartermaster Durn at Ashclaim Landing keeps the pay book, and he'll know whose number it is.",
        'You put the chit in a pocket by itself. Somebody at the landing is owed an answer.',
    ),
    'tmp_who_was_aboard': (
        "The log only lists the crew by rank. I'd like to know their names.\n\nEvery seaman carries a discharge book with his name and photograph in it. The murlocs took the log, so they've probably taken those as well.\n\nThe log puts the ship aground at the far south-east corner of the Tempest Shallows. She'll be the only steel wreck out there. See if she's there, and bring back any of the books you can find. These people have been missing for three years.",
        "Dry the books out slowly if they're wet. Pages stuck together are pages lost.",
    ),
    'tmp_empty_the_gatehouse': (
        "The first thing standing between us and the city is my great-grandfather's gatewarden.\n\nHis name was Hrun. He was holding the gate of Khaz Varun the night the city went dark, and he's still holding it. The gate opened by itself three years ago, on the day the world changed, and nobody I've sent in since has got past him.\n\nThe gate is on the south shore, a short walk south-east of Ashclaim Landing. Hrun is in the Gatehouse Hall past the Ember Road. He was a loyal dwarf, so make it quick.",
        'If his shield survives, bring it to me. It should hang in my hall.',
    ),
    'tmp_the_forge_lord': (
        "The squatters at the gate say the forge is lit, and they're right.\n\nThe Great Forge of Khaz Varun has been cold since before my father was born, and now it's burning. The rolls say the last Forge-Lord was a dwarf named Darrok who never left his anvil.\n\nThe Great Forge is on the east side of the city, past the Counting Hall. Whatever is working that anvil, I want it stopped before it's finished.",
        "Don't touch anything on the anvil when it's done. I'd like to see what it was making.",
    ),
    'tmp_thane_morrun': (
        "My great-grandfather was Morrun Ashhold, and he's still sitting in his chair at the top of the city.\n\nOne of the first party got as far as the Hall of Ashhold and saw him through the doors. He hasn't been a living dwarf for a long time. The squatters call him the Unmade.\n\nI can't take the city back while he's sitting in that chair. The hall is at the north end of the city, past the Shadow Gallery. I'm asking you to kill Thane Morrun the Unmade.",
        "Close the hall doors behind you when you leave. I'll open them myself when I'm ready.",
    ),
    'tmp_a_flame_for_each': (
        "I keep one flame on this terrace for everyone still down in the city, because I don't know their names.\n\nEvery Dark Iron of Khaz Varun carried a name-tablet, a small piece of iron with their name punched into it. The Ash-Wretches in the lower city were our people once, and some will still have their tablets.\n\nThe gate is on the south shore, south-east of Ashclaim Landing. The Ash-Wretches are in the Ash Pits and the Deep Way in the middle of the city. Bring me the tablets and I'll give each of them a flame.",
        "Bring every tablet you find, even the ones you can't read. I'll make out the names.",
    ),
    'tmp_the_iron_mask': (
        "There are dwarves in the city with iron masks riveted over their faces, and they weren't there before. Some of them are wearing Ashclaim boots, and I've lit flames on this terrace for people who wore those boots. Something in the Cells is taking the people who go in, masking them, and sending them out to preach. Those who've seen it call it The Iron Mask. The Cells are on the west side of Khaz Varun, below the Deep Way, so please go down and stop it before it takes anyone else.",
        "If any of them are still unmasked when you find them, bring them out. I'll light their flame myself.",
    ),
    'tmp_foundry_inventory': (
        "I've put money into a foundry I've never seen, and my partners want to know what state it's in.\n\nThe Thane says the works in Khaz Varun are sound. I'd like to hear that from someone who's actually stood in them.\n\nThe Smelter and the Great Forge are both on the east side of the city. The gate is on the south shore near Ashclaim Landing. Look them over for me. The Smelter still has its old master, Smelter-Master Vaud, and you'll need to get rid of him first.",
        'Count the furnaces that still hold heat. My partners care about that more than anything.',
    ),
    'tmp_what_masks_fetch': (
        "I've got a buyer on the mainland who collects Dark Iron work, and he wants the iron masks.\n\nThe Masked Zealots in Khaz Varun wear them riveted shut, and there's nothing else like them. I'd rather the Keeper didn't hear where they went.\n\nThe Zealots are all through the city from the Gatehouse Hall inward. The gate is on the south shore near Ashclaim Landing. I'll pay well for every mask.",
        'Bring them in a sack, not on your belt. People talk on this jetty.',
    ),
    'tmp_grandmothers_mark': (
        "My grandmother was the best armoursmith in Khaz Varun, and I've never seen any of her work.\n\nShe got out as a girl with nothing but her hammer. One of the Thane's people says there's a machine in the Workshop called The Crusher, plated with armour taken off the walls, and that one of the plates carries the Stonecast mark.\n\nThe Workshop is on the west side of the city, just past the Ember Road. I'd like that breastplate.",
        'Bring the whole plate, dents and all. I want to see how she shaped it.',
    ),
    'tmp_the_rolls_below': (
        "The Thane's claim rests on the rolls I keep, and one of them is missing.\n\nWhen the city went dark, the Deedkeeper of the day carried out the records of births and debts. He had to leave the Roll of Oaths, because it was chained to a desk in the Counting Hall. Without it I can't prove which families swore to the Ashholds.\n\nThe Counting Hall is in the middle of the city, past the Gatehouse Hall. I'm told Overseer Grall still walks his rounds with the roll on his belt.",
        "Bring the chain as well if it comes away. I'll need to show where it was fastened.",
    ),
    'tmp_what_they_breathed': (
        "People go into that city sane and come out raving, and I want to know if it's something in the air.\n\nIf it is, it matters to everyone here, because we're shipping ore out of the same rock. The Crazed Miners in the lower workings have been breathing it longest, and their clothes will be full of it.\n\nThe gate is on the south shore near Ashclaim Landing. The miners are in the Ember Road and the Borer Workings. Bring me the dust, and cover your mouth while you collect it.",
        "Shake the dust into the vials, don't scrape it. Scraping mixes in what's on the cloth.",
    ),
}
